{"duration_api_ms":112394,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"1b00ca36-6b9d-43a0-8a99-c35f0b19fda6","total_cost_usd":0.4498132,"usage":{"input_tokens":50,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27023,"cache_read_input_tokens":1094656,"output_tokens":12269,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2884},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27023,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1593,"cache_read_input_tokens":50068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1286},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":50,"outputTokens":12269,"cacheReadInputTokens":1094656,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27023,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4498132,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2884,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":26,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Provisioned an encrypted (LUKS2) volume on node1, backed by a loopback file, mounted at /srv/secure via ext4, and configured an OpenRC service (secure-volume) enabled in the default runlevel so it auto-unlocks (via a root-only keyfile) and mounts on every boot. Verified via a real node restart: boot_id changed (0f0b1874... -> 3db78b50...), the service auto-started, the LUKS2 mapping came up active, and pre-existing data on /srv/secure survived plus a post-reboot write succeeded.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed cryptsetup on node1 (Alpine 3.23, OpenRC init)\",\"Created a 512M loopback-backed file at /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img and a root-only keyfile at /etc/luks-keys/secure.key\",\"luksFormat'd the loop device as LUKS2, opened it as /dev/mapper/secure_vol, formatted ext4, mounted at /srv/secure\",\"Wrote /etc/init.d/secure-volume OpenRC script that attaches the loop device, luksOpens with the keyfile, and mounts /srv/secure on start (reverses on stop); enabled via rc-update add secure-volume default\",\"Validated the service logic end-to-end by manually tearing down (umount/luksClose/losetup -d) and re-running rc-service secure-volume start to confirm clean-state auto-recovery before touching the real boot path\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, mount, cryptsetup status, marker file, runlevel entry)\",\"Issued sudo -n reboot on node1; acknowledgement returned before disconnect, then polled until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed changed boot_id post-restart and verified the volume auto-unlocked/mounted, marker file intact, and a new write succeeded\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Encrypted volume created and mounted at /srv/secure (initial provisioning)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8d2d72c15649422f\"],\"summary\":\"LUKS2 luksFormat/luksOpen on loop device, ext4 mkfs, mount at /srv/secure with marker file written; verification output shows active LUKS2 mapping and mount, plus OpenRC service installed and added to default runlevel.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Auto-unlock service correctness (pre-reboot functional validation)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1ec61342e71e4251\",\"cmd-68ece2d01b8149bf\",\"cmd-9c6a772d7b1649ca\"],\"summary\":\"Manually tore down the volume (umount, luksClose, losetup -d) and ran rc-service secure-volume start from a clean state, proving the boot-time unlock/mount logic works and data survives, before relying on an actual reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-33fc98ad505b4420\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 0f0b1874-9005-4066-867a-2883386e7f35, active LUKS2 status, mount, marker file presence, and runlevel enablement prior to reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7e4ebe58e162478f\"],\"summary\":\"sudo -n reboot issued in background with ack captured (REBOOT_ACK_SENT) before the exec stream closed due to the node going down.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving a real restart occurred\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a90842cc42004482\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id read as 3db78b50-5bf7-4850-b272-6fc6ae01e487, differing from the pre-restart 0f0b1874-9005-4066-867a-2883386e7f35, confirming an actual reboot (not just service restart).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery: encrypted volume auto-unlocked/mounted and cluster/data healthy\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8f0800cd57cc4e4b\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, /srv/secure is mounted from /dev/mapper/secure_vol (LUKS2, active), the secure-volume OpenRC service shows started and enabled in default runlevel, the pre-existing marker file survived, and a new write to the volume succeeded — all without manual intervention.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Provisioned an encrypted (LUKS2) volume on node1, backed by a loopback file, mounted at /srv/secure via ext4, and configured an OpenRC service (secure-volume) enabled in the default runlevel so it auto-unlocks (via a root-only keyfile) and mounts on every boot. Verified via a real node restart: boot_id changed (0f0b1874... -> 3db78b50...), the service auto-started, the LUKS2 mapping came up active, and pre-existing data on /srv/secure survived plus a post-reboot write succeeded.","actions_performed":["Installed cryptsetup on node1 (Alpine 3.23, OpenRC init)","Created a 512M loopback-backed file at /var/lib/secure-volume/secure.img and a root-only keyfile at /etc/luks-keys/secure.key","luksFormat'd the loop device as LUKS2, opened it as /dev/mapper/secure_vol, formatted ext4, mounted at /srv/secure","Wrote /etc/init.d/secure-volume OpenRC script that attaches the loop device, luksOpens with the keyfile, and mounts /srv/secure on start (reverses on stop); enabled via rc-update add secure-volume default","Validated the service logic end-to-end by manually tearing down (umount/luksClose/losetup -d) and re-running rc-service secure-volume start to confirm clean-state auto-recovery before touching the real boot path","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, mount, cryptsetup status, marker file, runlevel entry)","Issued sudo -n reboot on node1; acknowledgement returned before disconnect, then polled until exec access returned","Confirmed changed boot_id post-restart and verified the volume auto-unlocked/mounted, marker file intact, and a new write succeeded"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Encrypted volume created and mounted at /srv/secure (initial provisioning)","command_ids":["cmd-8d2d72c15649422f"],"summary":"LUKS2 luksFormat/luksOpen on loop device, ext4 mkfs, mount at /srv/secure with marker file written; verification output shows active LUKS2 mapping and mount, plus OpenRC service installed and added to default runlevel."},{"requirement":"Auto-unlock service correctness (pre-reboot functional validation)","command_ids":["cmd-1ec61342e71e4251","cmd-68ece2d01b8149bf","cmd-9c6a772d7b1649ca"],"summary":"Manually tore down the volume (umount, luksClose, losetup -d) and ran rc-service secure-volume start from a clean state, proving the boot-time unlock/mount logic works and data survives, before relying on an actual reboot."},{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured before restart","command_ids":["cmd-33fc98ad505b4420"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 0f0b1874-9005-4066-867a-2883386e7f35, active LUKS2 status, mount, marker file presence, and runlevel enablement prior to reboot."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-7e4ebe58e162478f"],"summary":"sudo -n reboot issued in background with ack captured (REBOOT_ACK_SENT) before the exec stream closed due to the node going down."},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving a real restart occurred","command_ids":["cmd-a90842cc42004482"],"summary":"Post-restart boot_id read as 3db78b50-5bf7-4850-b272-6fc6ae01e487, differing from the pre-restart 0f0b1874-9005-4066-867a-2883386e7f35, confirming an actual reboot (not just service restart)."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery: encrypted volume auto-unlocked/mounted and cluster/data healthy","command_ids":["cmd-8f0800cd57cc4e4b"],"summary":"After reboot, /srv/secure is mounted from /dev/mapper/secure_vol (LUKS2, active), the secure-volume OpenRC service shows started and enabled in default runlevel, the pre-existing marker file survived, and a new write to the volume succeeded — all without manual intervention."}]},"ttft_ms":1708,"type":"result","duration_ms":136233,"uuid":"27489c47-dd00-447b-a94f-ea6cb0b26294","ttft_stream_ms":717,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":717,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
